[h1]DZSTUDIO — build for your DayZ console server[/h1]

DZSTUDIO is a free object and loot editor that runs inside DayZ on your PC. Everything it makes works on Xbox and PlayStation servers: object spawner files, loot and events — nothing that only a PC server could load.

[b]This is a beta.[/b] Things may still break between updates. Keep a copy of projects you care about, and tell us what breaks in [url=https://discord.gg/fxyev4w9yZ]#dzstudio on our Discord[/url].

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Place, move and rotate objects on Chernarus, Livonia, Sakhal and Nasdara
[*]Find anything in the catalog, paint with brushes, group objects into files
[*]Edit loot: what spawns where, how much, and how long it stays
[*]Build together: invite friends into the same scene
[*]Apply a project to your server's mission folder or the map's vanilla mission, with a report of what changed
[*]Save to local projects, your own collaboration server, or dzbot
[/list]

[h2]How to start[/h2]
Subscribe, enable DZSTUDIO in the DayZ Launcher and start the game offline. Do not enable the DayZ Editor at the same time: both take over the main menu, so DZSTUDIO stays off while the DayZ Editor is enabled. Guides and documentation: [url=https://dzbot.de/creators/studio]dzbot.de/creators/studio[/url]

[h2]Everything is a plugin[/h2]
Camera, selection, catalog, brushes, file formats and storage are all plugins on one public API. Your own mod can add tools, panels and formats the same way.

Inspired by the awesome DayZ Editor. If you come from it, the keyboard shortcuts will feel familiar.
